    <string name="settings_about_section_title">About these results</string>
    <string name="settings_about_how_it_works">Hue and You measures the color of clothing or an object from your photo, then compares it with the Best and Avoid colors in your profile using ΔE00, a perceptual color-difference formula.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_best_guess">This is our best guess, not a professional assessment. Seasonal color analysis — the idea that everyone has a best palette based on their skin, hair, and eye tone — has little scientific backing, so treat these results as a fun starting point rather than a verdict.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_delta_e">ΔE00 (\"Delta E 2000\") is a standard way to measure how different two colors look to the human eye: the higher the number, the more noticeable the difference.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_verdicts_intro">Rate Clothing gives each measured color one of three verdicts:</string>
    <string name="settings_about_verdict_yes">Great color! — the nearest Best color is close enough to count, and closer than anything you\'re avoiding.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_verdict_avoid">Avoid — the nearest color to avoid is close enough to count, and closer than your Best colors.</string>
    <string name="settings_about_verdict_neither">Ambiguous — nothing in your profile is close enough to call it either way.</string>

